          },
          "worked": "The supplied figure is a rotated $4\\times4$ square, so it contains $16$ dots. In the general pattern, the diagonal rows contain $1,2,\\ldots,n,\\ldots,2,1$ dots and form a rotated square with $n$ rows of $n$ dots.\n$$\\begin{align*}1+2+\\cdots+(n-1)+n+(n-1)+\\cdots+2+1&=n\\times n\\\\1+2+\\cdots+(n-1)+n+(n-1)+\\cdots+2+1&=n^2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
